Hecks.hecksagon "OutboundEvent" do
  uses_framework "Governance"
  # persistence : the outbox is event-sourced, so its Record / Claim /
  # MarkDelivered lifecycle rides the append-only Log (audit + replay + the
  # read model of undelivered deliveries). The bare `.event_sourced` verb
  # (zero args -> mints a Bind with adapter: "" -> `unknown adapter ""`
  # WiringError) was a Rust-era marker with no hecksagain equivalent ;
  # the fork already ships the real replacement as an ordinary
  # persistence-family adapter (see EventSourcing::Event.persisted_by
  # ("AppendLog") in event_sourcing.hecksagon for the identical pattern,
  # and framework/adapters/appendlog.adapter for the bind itself) -- one
  # bind, not persisted_by("Heki") PLUS a separate flag. i779 follow-up
  # (2026-08-17), category-2 cheap fix.
  OutboundEvent::OutboundEvent.persisted_by("AppendLog")
end
